  "mappingSource": "WinWing 3N.PDC.1 manual section 3.2 \"Buttons\" drawing (page 13 of the PDF, https://eu.winctrl.com/static/ipfs/QmUCdN2byoGPYV7Ayz82cEhLG96zQ48H6a4ZuDosFViZ9B), checked: matches the catalog (1 FPV, 2 MTRS, 3-9 WXR..TERR, 10/11/12 VOR 1/OFF/ADF 1, 13/14/15 VOR 2/OFF/ADF 2, 16 RST, 17 CTR, 18 TFC, 19 STD, 24/25 RADIO/BARO, 26/27 IN/HPA, 28-31 APP/VOR/MAP/PLN, 32-39 range 5..640, MINS spring knob 20/40/41/42/21, BARO spring knob 22/43/44/45/23); catalog also cites the X-Plane plugin Zibo PDC table (https://github.com/rswilem/winctrl-xplane-plugin)",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "MINS and BARO are stacked knobs: black push cap (RST / STD), front cream spring knob (slow 40/42 or 43/45 = rotary part; far positions 20/21 or 22/23 and centre 41 or 44 = button parts, all on that same knob), rear larger cream ring = RADIO/BARO or IN/HPA selector. The spring-knob position parts sit around the front knob (medium: one physical knob, several parts). The 3N has no VSD key (catalog has no panel.button.3).",
